  "equipment_type": "Generator set controller",
  "applies_to": "Cummins generator sets with PowerCommand 2.x or 3.x controls on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for Cummins PowerCommand 2.x/3.x: 81 objects (49 AI, 32 BI), all polled. It reads control switch position, latest fault code and type, the NFPA-style annunciator bits (common alarm, running, supplying load, not in auto, battery, coolant, oil, fuel, overspeed...), and genset voltage, current, kW, kVAR, PF, kVA and energy.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Cummins_PowerCommand_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the PowerCommand Modbus register map (Modbus 2300) (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/modbus2300.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 81 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Cummins_PowerCommand_a",
    "doc_number": "Cummins_PowerCommand_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/CumminsPowerCommand.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read Genset Running, Supplying Load, Not in Auto and Common Alarm, plus total kW. This profile is read-only; start/stop and mode stay on the genset panel or hard-wired remote start.",
